      "content": "thanks for the numbers, that's helpful. so if it's only a millimeter or two, that's still enough to notice, but it doesn't quite explain why some of the shifts look more like they were \"tossed\" or moved a few inches away from where they should be. \n\nif it's not just thermal expansion or floor vibration, could it be something with the pallet material itself or maybe even some kind of structural \"creep\" in the racking that's more sudden? i'm just trying to rule everything out before we call in a specialist.",
